w(f"Mapal's entry has 96 static `cvt.rna.tf32.f32` sites, beginning at {loc(p['path'],p['opcode_lines']['cvt.rna.tf32.f32'][0])}. Saved offline ptxas SASS contains 96 `IMAD.IADD.U32` sites and finite/Inf checks, with zero `F2FP` instructions; representative conversion sequence at {loc(s['path'],s['opcode_lines']['IMAD.IADD.U32'][0]-2)}. The pinned CUTLASS TF32 function has 96 `F2FP.TF32.F32.PACK_B` sites, first at {loc(c['path'],c['opcode_lines']['F2FP.TF32.F32.PACK_B'][0])}. The function's mangled name exactly matches the actual Nsight kernel record. Counts cover the static function, including loop/drain copies; they are not dynamic instruction counts.")
w('This is not a drop-in equivalent instruction replacement. Pinned CUTLASS `include/cutlass/gemm/warp/mma_tensor_op.h:363` chooses `PreferredRoundingMode`; `numeric_conversion.h:8358` defaults to nearest-even and selects half-ulp/truncate only for `__CUDA_ARCH__ < 900`; its nearest-even conversion uses `cvt.rn.tf32.f32` at line 647 on >=900. Mapal emits nearest-ties-away (`.rna`). NVIDIA documents the distinction and >=sm90 support for `.rn` TF32 conversion in the [PTX conversion specification](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/parallel-thread-execution/#data-movement-and-conversion-instructions-cvt). For the exactly representable FP32 halfway input `0x3f801000` = 1.00048828125, nearest-even produces 1.0 and nearest-away produces 1.0009765625; `verification.json` checks the exact scalar arithmetic, not a GPU execution.')
w('The current interim contract is specified in source: `crates/backends/llvm/src/lib.rs:408` documents `Reduced::Tf32` as operands rounded with `cvt.rna`. Accepted ADR-0032 requires bit-changing choices to belong to the language and forbids rounding changes via ambient backend config. ADR-0039 proposes explicit nearest-even `to_tf32` conversion, but is marked candidate / NOT decided. Consequently replacing `.rna` with `.rn` changes the current documented numeric face; it is not a value-invariant tuning change. A separately declared nearest-even experimental face could measure the opportunity, with midpoint, signed, subnormal, Inf/NaN and end-to-end checks, but results must remain labeled as a different numeric contract. Capture the actual driver-loaded image or load the tested cubin directly, and measure instruction/issue counts before attributing a performance gap to the conversion. The A100/4090 CUTLASS fatbins also use integer conversion sequences, so this is specifically a proven Blackwell distinction, not an explanation for the large A100 TF32 gap.')
